  "term": "mixed-methods research",
  "definition": "Mixed-methods research is an approach that combines different kinds of research methods, especially qualitative and quantitative ones, within a single study. In the packet’s example, this meant using qualitative content analysis together with linguistic analysis at the same time to study reflective writing.",
